{# ── Chapter: FE Depth ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="fe-depth">
  <h2>Scoping the observer and disconnecting when you're done</h2>
  <div class="tone-junior">
    <p>
      Watch as narrow a part of the page as you can, not the whole <code>document</code>, and set <code>subtree: true</code> only if you actually need to see changes in descendant elements too, not just direct children.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-mid">
    <p>
      Call <code>observer.disconnect()</code> once you've gotten the change you were waiting for, or in a cleanup function (a React effect's return, for example). An observer left running for the page's whole lifetime for a one-time check is its own kind of waste.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-staff">
    <p>
      For high-frequency mutation sources, batch your own handling inside the callback rather than reacting per mutation record; the callback already receives an array, so iterate once and derive the minimal update instead of triggering a re-render per individual DOM change.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

