{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">
    Don't poll the DOM on a timer for a change you're waiting for. MutationObserver tells you the moment it happens.
  </div>
        <div class="tone-mid">
    Scope the observer as narrowly as possible, and disconnect it once you've gotten what you needed.
  </div>
        <div class="tone-staff">
    Mutation callbacks are batched into microtasks and deliver an array of records, so handle them in one pass rather than reacting per mutation.
  </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
